From: dev0gig <115336867+dev0gig@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:59:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Local games do not create the network server manager

HostedMatch.startGame and InputPassPriority.showAndWait only ask whether
this process hosts a network game (isHosting, armAfkTimeout). Both called
FServerManager.getInstance(), which creates the manager on first use,
including two Netty NioEventLoopGroups (bossGroup, workerGroup) and the
network preferences. Every local game against the AI therefore built a
network server stack it never used.

New FServerManager.getInstanceIfCreated() returns the manager only if it
already exists. Both call sites use it: no manager means nothing is being
hosted, which is exactly what isHosting() == false / AfkTimeout.NOOP
already express. Hosting a network game is unaffected because that path
creates the manager through getInstance() before any of these checks.

This matters for single-threaded runtimes (GraalVM Web Image), which
cannot provide Netty's event loops, and it keeps network-play code out of
the local path.

Written for OpenMana on 2026-09-24.
---
 .../java/forge/gamemodes/match/HostedMatch.java     |  4 +++-
 .../gamemodes/match/input/InputPassPriority.java    |  3 ++-
 .../forge/gamemodes/net/server/FServerManager.java  | 13 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/HostedMatch.java b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/HostedMatch.java
index fafd9546..02332302 100644
--- a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/HostedMatch.java
+++ b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/HostedMatch.java
@@ -180,7 +180,9 @@ public class HostedMatch {
         // (It still subscribes to the Match bus for UiEvent sounds like blocker assignment.)
 
         // This logs game actions to NetworkLogConfig for debugging network games
-        if (FServerManager.getInstance().isHosting()) {
+        // OpenMana patch 0006: only ask an existing server manager; a local game must not create one.
+        final FServerManager serverManager = FServerManager.getInstanceIfCreated();
+        if (serverManager != null && serverManager.isHosting()) {
             game.subscribeToEvents(new NetworkGameEventListener());
         }
 
diff --git a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/input/InputPassPriority.java b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/input/InputPassPriority.java
index 1408fde8..d90afcbf 100644
--- a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/input/InputPassPriority.java
+++ b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/match/input/InputPassPriority.java
@@ -72,7 +72,8 @@ public class InputPassPriority extends InputSyncronizedBase {
 
     @Override
     public void showAndWait() {
-        final FServerManager server = FServerManager.getInstance();
+        // OpenMana patch 0006: only an existing server manager can host a game with AFK timeouts.
+        final FServerManager server = FServerManager.getInstanceIfCreated();
         final AfkTimeout timeout = server != null
                 ? server.armAfkTimeout(getController(), this)
                 : AfkTimeout.NOOP;
diff --git a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/net/server/FServerManager.java b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/net/server/FServerManager.java
index 3b67b1b7..800f53e8 100644
--- a/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/net/server/FServerManager.java
+++ b/forge-gui/src/main/java/forge/gamemodes/net/server/FServerManager.java
@@ -216,6 +216,19 @@ public final class FServerManager implements IHasForgeLog {
         return instance;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * The server manager if one was ever created, otherwise {@code null}.
+     * Never creates one.
+     *
+     * OpenMana patch 0006 (2026-09-24): code that only asks whether this
+     * process hosts a network game uses this, so a purely local game never
+     * constructs the manager and its Netty event loop groups (which a
+     * single-threaded runtime such as GraalVM Web Image cannot provide).
+     */
+    public static FServerManager getInstanceIfCreated() {
+        return instance;
+    }
+
     /**
      * Get the network byte tracker for monitoring actual bandwidth usage.
      *
